{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795608695,"nonce":"rZ8NvppVcSaDgfvCej7kGxJotJg=","title":"A linear or radial mask darkens an image twice","message":"`image.rs` (russl) multiplies a masked image's straight colour and its alpha by the mask, then premultiplies by the alpha, so the colour is scaled by the mask squared while the alpha is scaled once. A masked light image over a dark surface fades faster than its mask, and darkens over a light one.\n\nSeen while using the mask to fade SVG icons (the lane's light icons dim a little faster than the fade). Not fixed: image mask goldens were recorded with it.\n\nFix: multiply only the alpha by the mask, and re-record the mask goldens.","files":null}]}